# Performance Optimization Patterns

## React Performance Rules

### 1. Memoization

**Use React.memo() for expensive pure components:**
```typescript
export const ExpensiveComponent = memo<Props>(({ data }) => {
  return <div>{/* expensive rendering */}</div>;
});
```

**Use useMemo() for expensive calculations:**
```typescript
const sortedData = useMemo(() => {
  return data.sort((a, b) => a.value - b.value);
}, [data]);
```

**Use useCallback() for function props:**
```typescript
const handleClick = useCallback((id: string) => {
  // handler logic
}, []);
```

### 2. Code Splitting

**Use React.lazy() for route-based splitting:**
```typescript
const Dashboard = lazy(() => import('@/components/Dashboard'));

<Suspense fallback={<Loading />}>
  <Dashboard />
</Suspense>
```

**Use dynamic imports for large libraries:**
```typescript
// Only load when needed
const loadChart = async () => {
  const Chart = await import('chart.js');
  return Chart;
};
```

### 3. List Optimization

**Always use stable keys:**
```typescript
// ✅ Good - stable ID
{items.map(item => <Item key={item.id} {...item} />)}

// ❌ Bad - index as key
{items.map((item, i) => <Item key={i} {...item} />)}
```

**Virtualize long lists:**
```typescript
import { useVirtualizer } from '@tanstack/react-virtual';

const virtualizer = useVirtualizer({
  count: items.length,
  getScrollElement: () => parentRef.current,
  estimateSize: () => 50,
});
```

## Next.js Specific Optimizations

### Image Optimization
```typescript
import Image from 'next/image';

// Use priority for above-the-fold images
<Image src="/hero.jpg" alt="Hero" width={1200} height={600} priority />

// Lazy load below-the-fold
<Image src="/product.jpg" alt="Product" width={400} height={400} loading="lazy" />
```

### Font Optimization
```typescript
import { Inter } from 'next/font/google';

const inter = Inter({ subsets: ['latin'], display: 'swap' });

<main className={inter.className}>{children}</main>
```

### Caching Strategies
```typescript
// Static Generation with revalidation
export const revalidate = 3600; // 1 hour

// Fetch with caching
fetch(url, {
  next: { revalidate: 3600, tags: ['posts'] }
});
```

## Bundle Size Optimization

### Tree Shaking
```typescript
// ✅ Import only what you need
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/Button';

// ❌ Avoid barrel imports in large libraries
import { Button } from '@/components'; // May import everything
```

### Remove Unused Code
```typescript
// Remove console.logs in production
// next.config.js
compiler: {
  removeConsole: process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production',
}
```

## Performance Checklist

- [ ] Components memoized where beneficial
- [ ] Expensive calculations use useMemo
- [ ] Function props use useCallback
- [ ] Code splitting implemented
- [ ] Images optimized (next/image)
- [ ] Fonts optimized (next/font)
- [ ] Long lists virtualized
- [ ] Bundle size monitored
- [ ] Lazy loading for below-fold content
- [ ] No unnecessary re-renders

## When NOT to Optimize

- Don't memo everything (has overhead)
- Don't optimize before measuring
- Don't sacrifice readability for minimal gains
- Profile first, then optimize

